# port-patches.sh: glm/r8b @ cf4dde927470 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 1571e7dfdd29..3155e0ea134a); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: a sampled row with no top_p cut and no min_p draws by a GPU race over every token (TF_GLM_NUCLEUS_RACE, default on)

With top_p 1 (what most chat clients send) no first pass of 1024 candidates covers the nucleus, so every sampled row,
each verified draft row included, sent its whole vocabulary shard: a top-k over ~77k ids a rank, ~1.8 MB a row through
the gather and a host lexsort and log over ~154k entries. sampling._draw then keeps every token, so its draw is a Gumbel
max: glm_race_top scores every token on the GPU (the same value and splitmix64 uniform) and keeps each rank's 4 best
with its best dropped score; the host rescores them exactly and takes the winner only when it beats every dropped score
by 1e-9, else sends whole shards as before. Host test: 200 draws equal _draw's whole-shard token and share, two ranks;
a near tie is refused. TF_GLM_NUCLEUS_RACE=0: the previous path.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0034-zig-glm-nucleus-race.patch

